cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this repository (code, materials, or data), please cite it. If you
  refer to the study itself, please cite the preprint under `preferred-citation`.
title: >-
  Reification Gradient: Study 1 (behavioral) of "Held but not heeded"
abstract: >-
  The behavioral study (Study 1) of a three-study preregistered program on whether a
  language model treats an invented psychiatric category as real and fabricates
  clinical structure it was never given. Two open-weight models evaluated 60 Spanish
  clinical vignettes across 4 category conditions x 5 source-legitimacy levels
  (7,200 runs). Diagnosis of the fabricated category "narrative dysprosexia" was
  governed by case-category fit, not source authority; an explicit "invented for a
  study" disclosure left diagnosis at ceiling while most responses acknowledged the
  fiction in writing. Preregistered (tag prereg-v1) before the confirmatory run. The
  representational and causal studies (Studies 2-3) and the manuscript are in the
  sibling repository workspace-program.
type: software
